        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 33.6" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="565" ed="#liebermann"/>Augustinus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Hn_33-6.lnote.oe.12"/>: Iuris forensis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Hn_33-6.lnote.oe.13"/> est, qui in impeticionibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Hn_33-6.lnote.oe.14"/> mentitus est<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Hn_33-6.lnote.oe.15"/>, non ei prosit quod impetrauit.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 565 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page); Liebermann’s Erklärung (Gesetze III p. 321) has ‘fueril’ (an l for t; read ‘fuerit’); transcribed as printed</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_33-6.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">565</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-no <hi rend="italic">gegen Hss., Wi Tho</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-no <hi rend="italic">against the MSS, Wi Tho</hi></seg></note>
